"""Apply presentation edits while preserving numerical tables and study facts."""
from pathlib import Path

PARAGRAPHS = {
"These are **new experiments": "This study develops and evaluates a reproducible traffic-congestion forecasting framework using a reconstructed simulation dataset. Five model seeds, matched acquisition budgets and graph controls support the comparison of temporal, anomaly-aware and spatial modelling components. Source provenance and the initial data audit are documented in `REVISION_AUDIT_INITIAL.md`.",
"Unless stated otherwise": "Artifact paths refer to `reconstructed_v1/`, except where a root-relative path is stated. The root `results/` directory contains the source-data audit.",
"The full five-seed run selected": "The five-seed comparison selected A1 (plain LSTM) using the pre-specified mean validation-MAE criterion. Held-out accuracy was **74.8167 +/- 0.4406%**, MAE **4.7409 +/- 0.0217** and RMSE **6.3843 +/- 0.0199** on the 0-100 index. The main contribution is a reproducible evaluation of the integrated architecture and its component trade-offs under the defined simulation conditions.",
"Verification: **23 passed": "Verification completed with **23 checks passed**. Independent seed-42 A1 retraining reproduced all saved validation predictions exactly (maximum absolute difference 0.0). The initial source-data audit is retained separately for provenance.",
"- Fixed archived reconstructed": "- Fixed reconstructed simulation data; five model and selector seeds: [42, 123, 456, 789, 1024]. These seeds vary model fitting and sample selection while holding the generated dataset constant.",
"- Hourly sensor means": "- Hourly sensor means, causal forward fill, train-node median initialization and 14 documented features. Chronology uses the reconstructed ordinal hourly index.",
"- Unique initial-training": "- Unique initial-training input hours 0..4430 fit the scaler, imputation medians and proxy quantiles. AE early stopping uses an internal training holdout; its evaluation threshold is fixed at 0.015.",
"- New features, in order": "- Features, in order: speed_kmh, travel_delay_min, acceleration_ms2, gps_speed_noise_kmh, sensor_count, hour_sin, hour_cos, weekday_sin, weekday_cos, peak_indicator, rolling_ratio_mean_12, rolling_ratio_std_12, volume_intensity_veh_h_per_km, volume_capacity_ratio.",
"The Nigerian route-context file": "The experimental input is the supplied reconstructed segment dataset. Original Nigerian route-context records and the original Metro time series were outside the available experimental inputs. Hour and day indicators follow the reconstructed ordinal chronology. Each forecast uses past observations, with all fitted preprocessing parameters fixed from the initial training partition.",
"For Equation 12, use": "The GCN uses `B_ij = 1[A_ij + A_ji > 0]`, `A_hat = B + I`, `d_i = sum_j A_hat_ij`, and `A_norm_ij = A_hat_ij / sqrt(d_i*d_j)`. Each neighborhood includes the node itself once. Graph layers compute `ReLU(A_norm H W + b)`, followed by training-time dropout and a linear node readout. A separate directed graph represents routing transitions.",
"A5 in this contribution ablation": "A5 represents the pre-specified final entropy-acquisition stage, `A5_entropy_885`, with 885 acquired snapshots. Final-model selection considers all eligible configurations under the same validation criterion. Raw graph-row inference times refer to the graph head; complete A4 pipeline timing is reported separately. Pipeline parameter counts appear in `benchmark/params_runtime.csv`.",
"HA/Persistence/ARIMA are deterministic": "HA, persistence and ARIMA produce deterministic predictions on the fixed dataset, giving zero between-seed variation. ARIMA parameters are fitted on training data; its fixed-parameter state filter updates using observed past validation values for one-step forecasting.",
"The intervals use 2,000": "The 95% intervals use 2,000 circular 24-hour block resamples, retaining all 20 nodes together. They describe held-out sampling uncertainty conditional on the five fitted models. Exact per-seed metrics and prediction fingerprints appear in `final_eval/`.",
"Original-topology superiority": "The original graph and degree-preserving controls produced comparable results under the corrected paired tests; superiority of the original topology was not established across MAE, RMSE and SCS. The simulated segments share a temporal driver, and the GCN represents undirected neighborhood adjustment.",
"No corrected lower-budget": "Entropy and random sampling showed comparable lower-budget accuracy under the corrected tests. Additional acquisition and refinement reduced the full pipeline's final-stage errors relative to its initial state.",
"Both selectors use the same": "Both selectors share the initial model, acquisition pool, oracle, validation set, ten-epoch LSTM and GCN refinement schedule, and stage-wise optimizer resets. At the final budget, both have acquired the entire pool; differences then reflect the training path. Because validation precedes acquisition chronologically, it serves as a fixed retrospective selection set after refinement. The later final test provides temporal generalization assessment.",
"Ordinal distance-to-class-center": "Ordinal distance-to-class-center entropy ranks samples by class-boundary ambiguity. Acquisition cost is expressed as queried network snapshots and the corresponding simulated node-label count.",
"The targets are deterministically": "The simulated oracle supplies congestion targets calculated from generated volume and study capacity. Labels are withheld according to the acquisition protocol, providing a controlled setting for comparing sample-selection strategies. The resulting budget measures simulated label access rather than human annotation effort.",
"AE results are agreement": "AE metrics quantify agreement with the hourly proxy rule. Validation contains **4 proxy positives among 11,780 node-hours**. Recall was high, while low precision and F1 show that the fixed 0.015 threshold generated many additional alerts. These findings identify threshold calibration and richer anomaly scenarios as priorities for further development.",
"STGCN-lite is a disclosed": "STGCN-lite uses one temporal-gated / first-order graph / temporal-gated block with 32 channels. Two width-three temporal kernels and latest-position readout yield a five-hour effective receptive field. It is a reduced architectural comparator evaluated on validation data; broader benchmarking would require full-scale STGCN, DCRNN and Graph WaveNet implementations.",
"STGCN-lite had lower mean": "STGCN-lite achieved mean validation MAE 4.8923, compared with 4.9004 for A5. Parameter counts were 10,049 and 211,960, respectively, illustrating the accuracy and model-size trade-offs in this comparison.",
"Matched workload CPU timings": "The accompanying CPU measurements compare A4 and STGCN-lite under the same input workload.",
"CPU-only PyTorch was available.": "CPU inference profiling gave an A4 mean batch-one p95 of **10.489 ms** per 20-segment network update. Seed-wise mean, standard deviation and percentile timings for A4 and STGCN-lite appear in `latency/`. Batch20 represents 20 networks, or 400 segment sequences. The measured path includes engineered-window JSON decoding, float conversion, train-fitted scaling and model inference. Sensor transport, rolling-feature maintenance and dashboard rendering are outside this measurement.",
"If p95 is below": "The measured CPU inference path was compatible with the five-minute update cycle under the tested engineered-window workload.",
"Paired two-sided t tests": "Paired two-sided t tests compare the five model seeds, with Holm correction within each comparison family and paired Cohen dz effect sizes. The ten rewires per seed are averaged before testing. Interpretation combines effect sizes, observed variability and corrected significance; five seeds provide a limited estimate of between-run variability. For deterministic classical baselines, paired variation comes from neural-model fitting.",
"See `results/claim_support_matrix.csv`": "Detailed comparisons appear in `results/claim_support_matrix.csv`, `ablation/paired_tests.csv`, `graph_validity/significance_tests.csv`, `active_learning/paired_tests_entropy_vs_random.csv` and `benchmark/significance_vs_proposed.csv`. The tables in this report form a consistent results set for the simulation methods described here.",
"`reconstructed_v1/protocol/` contains": "The release includes the fixed protocol and SHA256 hashes, model-ready dataset, trained checkpoints, seed-specific predictions, epoch logs, evaluation tables and figures. Validation predictions cover all comparisons; test predictions cover the selected configuration. These materials are packaged locally in `Reconstructed_Study_Results_and_Reproducibility.zip`. Public deposition and a permanent identifier remain future release steps.",
"The original manuscript's web-dashboard": "The present evaluation covers forecasting, anomaly scoring, graph adjustment, acquisition and model-inference timing. Dashboard injection tests and routing-event benchmarks require a separate application-level evaluation using the corresponding source code and event logs."
}

def polish(text):
    lines=text.splitlines()
    for i,line in enumerate(lines):
        for prefix,replacement in PARAGRAPHS.items():
            if line.startswith(prefix):
                lines[i]=replacement
                break
    text="\n".join(lines)+"\n"
    if Path('REVIEWER_BENCHMARK_RESULTS.md').exists():
        text=text.replace('broader benchmarking would require full-scale STGCN, DCRNN and Graph WaveNet implementations.', 'The full STGCN, DCRNN and Graph WaveNet comparisons are now reported in the root-level `REVIEWER_BENCHMARK_RESULTS.md`.')
        if '## Full-architecture benchmark extension' not in text:
            text += "\n## Full-architecture benchmark extension\n\nThe reviewer-requested STGCN, DCRNN and Graph WaveNet comparisons are complete: 15 full-architecture fits, 30 prediction files and seven additional checks. The root-level `REVIEWER_BENCHMARK_RESULTS.md` reports their methods, paired comparisons and matched CPU timings. STGCN achieved validation MAE 4.6555 +/- 0.0259, DCRNN 4.6942 +/- 0.0253 and Graph WaveNet 4.7072 +/- 0.0393 index points. MAE differences between A1 and each benchmark were not significant after Holm correction. The extended comparison retains the original A1 selection and labels reuse of the previously examined temporal test as retrospective.\n"
    return text.replace("# New reconstructed-data simulation: measured revision results", "# Traffic-congestion forecasting: experimental methods and results").replace("## Main revision finding", "## Principal findings").replace("## Locked study and data accounting", "## Study design and data").replace("## Actual software timing", "## Inference performance").replace("## Statistics and claim support", "## Statistical analysis").replace("## AE and benchmark interpretation", "## Anomaly detection and architectural comparison")

if __name__=='__main__':
    for p in [Path('REVISION_RESULTS.md'),Path('reconstructed_v1/RECONSTRUCTED_RESULTS.md')]:
        before=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');after=polish(before)
        assert [s for s in before.splitlines() if s.startswith('|')]==[s for s in after.splitlines() if s.startswith('|')]
        p.write_text(after,encoding='utf-8')
